          "content": {
            "heading": "TRANSLUCENCY AND WEIGHT",
            "description": "To balance the heavy, protective outerwear that defines the season, we introduced elements of extreme fragility. Silk organza, woven so finely it resembles spun glass, acts as a counterpoint to the dense Melton wools. It is a study in contrasts—vulnerability shielded by armor."
